From da080472c7fb3028f41885aa93b3fbb2d519175f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 20:13:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sharding: relative intent TTLs, storm-brake withdrawals,
 delay grows in test view

- Intent messages carry a relative ttl_us; receivers count an intent for
  that long from arrival, so clock skew cannot void it early. The sender's
  expiry still identifies the intent for withdrawals. Lifetimes are capped
  at one hour. Senders without the field keep the absolute expiry.
- The storm brake withdraws the intents it cancels, as a stand-down does.
- The test-only view delay now applies to grow intents as well.
